# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# N. THE NOTIFYING EDGES — a subset by policy, not by oversight (#1346)
#
# core/domain/notify's push policy divides the vocabulary in two: `waiting`,
# `ready` and `error` are edges that produce a notification, and `working` is
# not, because entering work is never news to a phone (§8.4 of
# docs/mobile-notifications-arc42.md). Every site below names the notifying
# three on one line for that reason, so completing the list would make each of
# them WRONG rather than more complete.
#
# This is not a deferral and there is nothing tracking it. A fifth state does
# have to be decided about here, but the decision is "does it notify", not "add
# it to the list" — and that decision is enforced elsewhere, by
# TestEveryCanonicalStateHasADecidedPolicy in vocabulary_test.go, which fails
# on a canonical state the engine has no recorded policy for. That test is the
# reason this waiver is safe; without it, waiving these sites would be exactly
# the silence that let `error` reach production notifying nobody.

core/domain/notify/engine.go        the three NOTIFYING edges; `working` is excluded by policy (§8.4)
core/domain/notify/storm_test.go    the oracle grades those same three edges (§8.4)
